WEBVTT

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:04.730
It's time for today's greatest Riding Duel!

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.570
He's coming!  Everybody listen!

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:14.640
King of D-Wheelers Jack Atlas!

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.590
Sorry to keep you waiting!  I'm the King!

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:16.870
No matter how far apart we 
are, we can’t be stopped

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:21.930
That’s deeply engraved into us

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:30.470
So don’t be afraid of getting hurt

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:36.410
Break through even further

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:41.950
While carrying your beliefs in your heart

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:49.060
There’s always only one truth

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:52.920
So feel the voice of your heart

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:57.730
With your unwavering emotions,

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:03.840
Seize the signs of tomorrow

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:39.360
Riding Duel!  Acceleration!

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:45.560
It's the 143rd Duel King Competition.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:54.140
Will the challenger Mukuro Enjo be able 
to beat the undefeated ultimate deck?

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:59.330
How will the King face the enemy's challenge?

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:03.610
Watch the battle of destiny!

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:08.360
The time has come to place 
a spell on the field!

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:15.010
The challenger is next to the King.  
Set on the Field Spell Speed World!

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:18.710
Duel mode on.  Autopilot standby.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.840
The field is now under the 
control of Speed World!

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:28.730
Now spells other than Speed 
Spells cannot be activated!

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:32.260
Speed Spells are the most unique 
feature of Riding Duels.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:36.780
They are spell cards that can only be 
activated when Speed World covers the field.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:39.770
The activation requirements are 
different than Normal Spells.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:43.770
They are determined by the 
number of Speed Counters.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:47.780
In other words, the duelist's 
speed itself becomes spells!

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:50.770
The starter signal has appeared, 
and it's showing red.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:54.880
Now!  Riding Duel acceleration!

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:56.980
The challenger goes first!

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:58.830
Here I go!

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:09.750
The challenger Mukuro Enjo is assaulting 
the King with a clever trap!

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:13.310
However, the King isn't 
backing down!  What's this?

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:16.840
I'll show you my great power!

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:23.910
It's appeared!  The King's main 
monster RED DRAGON ARCHFIEND!

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.870
This is my thanks for giving me a fun time.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:31.200
I'll give you the honor of 
falling prey to our fangs.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.310
Take this!

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:38.350
Scorching Crimson Hellflare!

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:12.640
The King has successfully 
protected his throne again!

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:14.870
Jack!  Jack!  Jack!

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:16.280
A new page has been added 
to his undefeated legend!

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:20.190
There's only one King!  It's me!

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:52.300
In the beginning, it appeared as if you 
were troubled by the challenger's trap.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:56.480
However, you were actually thinking 
two or three moves ahead.

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:02.990
If the King used his full strength from the 
beginning, it would have been over in an instant.

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:07.030
The King's duel must be entertaining!

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.890
Hey, Yusei.

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:23.730
Sorry.  We couldn't help 
but be interested in Jack.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:25.720
And the TV only works in here.

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:27.850
He was amazing.

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:29.890
He's even stronger than before.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.510
His opponent was weak, right?

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:41.720
Yeah, he was completely played by Jack.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.830
He's bored.

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:50.950
What's the status of the D-Wheel?

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:53.020
Be quiet!  Can't you tell by looking?

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:54.620
That's right...

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.430
How is Jack's former D-Wheel performing?

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:58.820
Can't you sense the mood?

00:06:58.310 --> 00:06:59.240
Ouch!

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:04.030
But everyone is angry at Jack.

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:09.180
Yusei should have been King at that stadium!

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:15.000
But that punk Jack stole the 
D-Wheel that Yusei built!

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:22.530
Yusei!

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:26.570
Hi Rally.

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:27.740
Hey.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:30.420
Oh, everyone's here.  Yusei!

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.580
Why are you in such a hurry?

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:37.760
Can you use this for your D-Wheel?

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:39.060
What is that?

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:41.510
Hey!

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:45.890
This is brand new!  Where did you get it?

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:50.070
You have it all wrong. I 
found it among the junk.

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:55.170
You didn't steal again, did you?

00:07:56.370 --> 00:08:00.330
If that's stolen, then all 
of us might get arrested.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:05.060
We don't want to wear this mark.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:06.520
Stop.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:14.290
I'll use it.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.350
Are you sure, Yusei?

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:21.520
It'll definitely run faster!

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:33.030
Yusei, I know how you feel, 
but forget about Jack.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:36.350
Yusei is going to settle things with Jack!

00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:42.780
But in order to do that, he'll have 
to face many dangers.  Is it worth it?

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:47.170
But Jack stole Yusei's main monster!

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:51.080
Yusei, are you seriously going to leave here?

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:54.640
I'm not leaving.  I'm just going.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:58.570
Don't do it.  That place isn't for us.

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:02.770
From the beginning, Jack 
was different than us.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:20.080
So?  It's totally better, right?

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:25.080
Go for a ride!  It's really fast!

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.390
What is it?

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:30.790
It's Security!

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:37.860
Identification number 
AWX 86007, Rally Dawson!

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:40.760
You're under suspicion for 
robbery.  Surrender immediately!

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:45.790
Come out!  As long as you have 
a marker, you can't escape!

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:47.190
You…

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:50.940
Sorry!  I took it from the factory.

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:54.850
Because I wanted Yusei to beat Jack!

00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:56.130
That's no excuse!

00:09:57.770 --> 00:09:58.810
That's enough.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.670
That's you being you!

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:05.220
As long as you have a marker, you can't 
escape.  It sends a signal to Security.

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:12.790
What?  The signal's been severed!

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:16.200
I've severed the marker signal.

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:17.550
You jammed it?

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:19.230
Everyone, go over there.

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:22.120
I'll draw Security's attention.

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:27.070
We're also leaving!

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:34.910
A D-Wheel?

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:37.330
The suspect is fleeing!  After him!

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:47.030
It's fast.

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:50.490
The front and rear wheel outputs, the 
balance control of the rotations...

00:10:50.490 --> 00:10:51.390
It's perfect.

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:56.470
D-Wheel, it's no use trying to escape!  Stop!

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:19.310
Where did you steal that D-Wheel from?

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:26.110
You don't have a marker.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:30.420
So you're a decoy.  I guess 
garbage helps other garbage.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:37.460
You will be arrested for 
aiding in the escape.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:41.980
I also want to know where 
you got that D-Wheel from.

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:42.670
Hey.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:45.840
Let's duel.

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:50.830
A piece of garbage from 
Satellite wants to duel me?

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:53.970
You don't even have cards.  
Stop making me laugh.

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:56.840
I found cards.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:04.420
If I win, you forget about 
everything that happened today.

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:07.450
There's no way we can do that!

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:10.930
You talk big.  I accept.

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:13.350
Ushio, you can't do this.

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:16.110
I'll take the responsibility.  
You guys go home.

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:17.500
Ushio!

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:21.940
Go.  Or do you think I'm going to lose?

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:24.510
Sheesh.

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:34.030
You're an interesting man.

00:12:34.030 --> 00:12:35.570
What do you mean?

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:38.150
I don't trust Security.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:41.320
But a duelist...  That's a different story.

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:46.150
You accepted this duel, so I'll trust you.

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:48.790
You're so annoying.

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:57.610
Let's go.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:01.970
I set the Field Spell SPEED WORLD.

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:06.300
Duel mode on.  Autopilot standby.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:10.160
Duel!

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.420
I'll go first.

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:36.870
I summon Assault Dog!

00:13:39.190 --> 00:13:42.220
Then I set a card and end my turn!

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:47.110
My turn.

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:50.060
I summon Speed Warrior.

00:13:55.800 --> 00:14:02.080
In attack position.  However, it has nowhere 
near the attack points of my Assault Dog!

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:09.040
The attack points doubled?

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:11.490
Speed Warrior's attack points 
are doubled only during

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:14.490
the Battle Phase of the turn 
in which it was summoned.

00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:18.420
How annoying when all you are is garbage!

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:20.820
Speed Warrior!

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.260
Sonic Edge!

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:36.500
Not bad.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:38.650
But I have a monster effect also!

00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:48.110
When Assault Dog is sent to 
the graveyard due to battle,

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:52.110
I can Special Summon another 
Assault Dog from my deck!

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:56.120
I set one card and end my turn.

00:14:59.150 --> 00:15:00.320
My turn!

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:02.790
I release Assault Dog!

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:06.780
I Advance Summon my Level 
5 monster Handcuffs Dragon!

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:12.950
Handcuffs Dragon!  Handcuff Shoot!

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:15.210
I activate my trap.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:17.070
Scrap-Iron Scarecrow.

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:23.850
This negates your monster's attack.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:26.850
That's not a bad move.  However…

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:29.160
The trap card Wiretap!

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:34.210
This card negates the activation of your 
trap card and returns it to your deck.

00:15:34.690 --> 00:15:36.870
Do it, Handcuffs Dragon!

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:45.380
If it's a deck you made 
from cards that you found,

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:48.380
then no matter how you built 
it, it's still garbage!

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:51.360
My turn.

00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:53.860
I summon Sonic Chick in defense position.

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.660
Then I set two cards and end my turn.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:05.790
Your entire battle strategy is just 
to defend.  You're just all talk!

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:07.200
My turn!

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:11.590
Here I go!

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:14.140
Level 4, Level 3, Level 3.

00:16:14.590 --> 00:16:19.330
By sending these three cards in my hand to 
the graveyard, I Special Summon Montage Dragon!

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:29.450
Due to this card's monster effect, 
its attack points are equal to the

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:33.150
sum of the Levels of the monsters I sent 
to the graveyard multiplied by 300!

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:36.920
3000…

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.670
Handcuffs Dragon attacks Sonic Chick!

00:16:40.670 --> 00:16:42.290
Handcuff Shoot!

00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:46.310
Sonic Chick…

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.590
The main event is now about to begin!

00:16:48.590 --> 00:16:51.970
Montage Dragon, attack the player directly!

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:53.540
Power Collage!

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:06.510
My speed…  It's due to the 
effect of the direct attack.

00:17:07.180 --> 00:17:10.420
You only have 100 life points 
remaining, you garbage!

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:16.930
My cards, I believe in you.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:18.450
Answer my voice.

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:23.180
It arrived.

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:26.610
I summon the Tuner Monster Junk Synchron.

00:17:32.240 --> 00:17:35.030
A Tuner Monster?  It can't be!

00:17:35.590 --> 00:17:36.970
It is.

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:40.620
I activate the trap card Graceful Revival!

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:47.900
With this card, I can Special Summon one 
Level 2-or-below monster in my graveyard.

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:50.900
Come, Speed Warrior!

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:52.310
What?

00:17:58.850 --> 00:18:01.720
Junk Synchron tunes Speed Warrior!

00:18:13.310 --> 00:18:17.040
The stars come together 
to call forth a new power!

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:18.790
Become the path that lights the way!

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:21.320
Synchro Summon!

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:24.800
Come, Junk Warrior!

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:32.080
No way!

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:35.170
This Satellite garbage was 
able to Synchro Summon?

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:39.740
Still, it can't stand up to 
Montage Dragon's attack points!

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:43.300
Activate Speed Spell!

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:44.660
Vision Wind!

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:46.380
Speed Spell?

00:18:46.380 --> 00:18:50.290
I diminished that punk's speed 
by attacking him directly.

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:51.750
How dare he do that!

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:57.870
With this card, I can Special Summon one 
Level 2-or-below monster in my graveyard.

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:04.650
I Special Summon Level 2 Speed Warrior!

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:07.700
Then Junk Warrior's monster effect activates.

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:15.390
The attack points of a Level 2-or-below 
monster on my field are added to Junk Warrior.

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:20.300
With a Speed Spell combo, you instantly 
increased your attack points!

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:21.530
How annoying.

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:28.120
Go, Junk Warrior.  Attack Handcuffs Dragon!

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:30.590
Scrap Fist!

00:19:35.670 --> 00:19:40.990
You chose to attack Handcuffs Dragon because you 
preferred to damage me, but now you've lost the battle!

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:50.950
See that?  When Handcuffs 
Dragon is destroyed in battle,

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:53.880
it becomes an equip card that 
is equipped to your monster,

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:56.880
and your monster loses attack 
points equal to its attack points.

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:58.530
Now it's over!

00:19:58.530 --> 00:20:01.780
From the beginning, you aren't 
able to disobey authority!

00:20:02.150 --> 00:20:04.980
I will use that monster 
effect to my advantage.

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:05.910
What?

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:09.670
I activate the trap card Equip Shot.

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:19.350
Montage Dragon's attack points are...!

00:20:19.770 --> 00:20:24.800
Equip Shot is a card that re-equips an 
equip card on to the opponent's monster.

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:29.630
The monsters targeted by 
this effect now battle.

00:20:31.150 --> 00:20:32.480
Junk Warrior!

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:38.990
Scrap Fist!

00:20:50.260 --> 00:20:55.390
I can't believe it.  I 
lost to this garbage...

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:03.980
No matter what the card is, as long as 
it exists, it has the power to be useful.

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:07.070
You don't have the right to call yourself a

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:10.070
duelist when you dismiss cards 
by calling them garbage.

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:18.550
I will crush you!

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:41.170
Just wait, Jack.

00:22:05.440 --> 00:22:10.970
What can we grasp?  What can we do?

00:22:11.370 --> 00:22:16.380
We’ll step forward and find out

00:22:16.780 --> 00:22:22.320
My unstoppable emotions, the 
beating of my passionate heart

00:22:22.490 --> 00:22:27.560
I heard the voice of truth

00:22:27.760 --> 00:22:30.730
After I was hurt, I learned

00:22:33.300 --> 00:22:36.300
Of a place where I can become stronger

00:22:38.270 --> 00:22:43.470
I stack my dreams in my palm

00:22:43.610 --> 00:22:48.880
And I’ll someday pass them to you

00:22:49.310 --> 00:22:54.820
Seeking for the signal 
to start, my soul roars

00:22:55.120 --> 00:23:00.060
I will overcome my suffocating 
and mediocre life

00:23:00.690 --> 00:23:06.200
I’ll dash and acquire 
all the bright futures

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:15.610
Carrying the bonds I believe 
in, I run towards tomorrow
